      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/17/addison-lee-founder-owes-tax-after-uk-tribunal-ruling",
      "description": "<p>HMRC wins challenge over John Griffin’s claim to be non-dom despite having lived in England since childhood</p><p>The founder of Addison Lee owes £20.5m in tax after a tribunal dismissed a claim that he should be treated as a nom-dom despite living in the UK since childhood.</p><p>John Griffin had argued he should be treated as a nom-dom due to his connection to Ireland, saying: “I was and am besotted with Ireland, infatuated with Ireland. I believe that I have always been and am Irish.”</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/17/addison-lee-founder-owes-tax-after-uk-tribunal-ruling\">Continue reading...</a>",
